      "Language": "cze",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors describe the case of a 46-year-old patient with serious manifestations of ischaemic heart disease-repeated myocardial infarctions, malignant arrhythmias, the algic form of angina pectoris, whose complaints were markedly linked to the menstrual cycle. The authors mention also the individual solution, i.e. elimination of ovarian activity by actinotherapy."},
